The given key does not identify an element in this collection value: the collection has no elements.

Failed Command:
terraform apply -auto-approve -input=false

Root Cause Analysis:
This test case is a "cleanup" test that depends on previous test cases (diskOSImportManagedDisk and diskOSImportManagedDiskWithSize) to have created a managed disk first. The configuration uses a data source `data.azurerm_managed_disks.test` to query for existing managed disks in the resource group, then references the first disk via `disk.0.id`.

Since this test is run in isolation without the prerequisite tests having been executed (both prerequisite tests are marked as "invalid" in test_cases.md), the data source returns an empty list, causing the index error.

Conclusion:
This is not a valid standalone test case - it's a helper/cleanup test that depends on other tests. It should only be run as part of a test suite where the prerequisite tests execute first. Since the prerequisite tests (diskOSImportManagedDisk and diskOSImportManagedDiskWithSize) are both marked as "invalid", this cleanup test cannot be executed.

Test Status: Invalid (dependent test case, cannot run standalone)
